Returning a value 
• Up to one value may be returned; it must be the same type as 
the return type. 
• If no values are returned, give the function a void return type 
void printNumber(int num) { 
  cout << "number is " << num << endl; 
} 

int main() { 
  printNumber(4); // number is 4 
  return 0; 
