Deep copy 
Deep copy dynamically allocates the memory for the copy and then copies the actual value, both the 
source and copy have distinct memory locations. In this way, both the source and copy are distinct 
and will not share the same memory location. Deep copy requires us to write the user-defined 
constructor. 
