AVL Tree 

AVL(Adelson, Velski & Landis,) tree is a height-balanced binary search tree. That means, 
an AVL tree is also a binary search tree but it is a balanced tree. A binary tree is said to be 
balanced if, the difference between the heights of left and right subtrees of every node in the 
tree is either -1, 0 or +1. In other words, a binary tree is said to be balanced if the height of 
left and right children of every node differ by either -1, 0 or +1. In an AVL tree, every node 
maintains an extra information known as balance factor.

