Returning Value from a Subroutine 
You can return a value from subroutine like you do in any other programming 
language. If you are not returning a value from a subroutine then whatever 
calculation is last performed in a subroutine is automatically also the return value. 

You can return arrays and hashes from the subroutine like any scalar but returning 
more than one array or hash normally causes them to lose their separate identities. 

Let's try the following example, which takes a list of numbers and then returns their 
average  

#!/usr/bin/perl 
#Function definition 
sub Average{

# get total number of arguments passed. 
$ n = scalar(@ _); 
$ sum = 0; 
foreach $ item (@ _){ 
$ sum += $ item ; 
} 
$ average = $ sum / $ n; 
return $ average; 
